            <ArticleTitle>[The correlations of lipid peroxidation, antioxidant protection and microrheological disorders in the development of IHD].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>37-40</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Lipid peroxidation, antioxidant defense and microrheological properties of blood were determined, correlated and compared with clinico-hemodynamic indices in patients with ischemic heart disease (IHD). It is shown that products of lipid peroxidation modify structure and function of red cells and platelets in IHD. A regulatory role of the antioxidant system in metabolism of lipoperoxides and peroxide damage to blood cells in IHD is shown. A pathogenetic implication of correlated changes in the systems of lipid peroxidation and antioxidant defense, microrheological properties of blood in formation of clinical course of IHD is revealed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
